   "text": "This SMILES is read from the drawing. The macrocycle is a peptide closed by a thioether, and I traced the ring residue by residue from the glycinamide end.\n\n**Sequence, in the order the amide bonds run around the ring:**\n- Gly-NH2 is the C-terminal amide.\n- Cys is attached to Gly through its C=O, and its side-chain sulfur forms the thioether S\u2013CH2\u2013C(=O) to the N-terminus of the next residue.\n- Phe, Arg, N-Me-Phe, Ser, Val, Asn, Tyr, Lys, Arg, Asp follow in that order.\n- Tic (tetrahydroisoquinoline-3-carboxylic acid, a cyclic amino acid whose ring nitrogen is acylated by Asp) comes next.\n- Asn and N-Me-Phe follow, and the N-Me-Phe carbonyl closes the ring onto the Cys nitrogen.\n- Each Arg side chain ends in a guanidine, and the Asp side chain is a free carboxylic acid.\n\n**Stereochemistry:** I worked out each alpha-carbon from its wedge or hash and the CIP priorities. Every residue comes out L (S, or R for Cys because of the sulfur) except Val, whose hashed isopropyl gives D-Val. The upper Asn is read as L on the assumption that its side-chain bond is a wedge, since the bond is hard to make out in the image.\n\nSMILES: NC(=O)CNC(=O)[C@@H]1CSCC(=O)N[C@@H](Cc2ccccc2)C(=O)N[C@@H](CCCNC(=N)N)C(=O)N(C)[C@@H](Cc2ccccc2)C(=O)N[C@@H](CO)C(=O)N[C@H](C(C)C)C(=O)N[C@@H](CC(N)=O)C(=O)N[C@@H](Cc2ccc(O)cc2)C(=O)N[C@@H](CCCCN)C(=O)N[C@@H](CCCNC(=N)N)C(=O)N[C@@H](CC(=O)O)C(=O)N2Cc3ccccc3C[C@H]2C(=O)N[C@@H](CC(N)=O)C(=O)N(C)[C@@H](Cc2ccccc2)C(=O)N1"
